From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 05:24:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 281/283] chore(execution): bump region plan schema to v2 and
 structure empty-operations refusal

Round-3 items for verify-0049-u5-region, based on integration tip b643229bd.

* REGION_SCHEMA_VERSION 1 -> 2: the round-2 anchoring change made the
  region_digest preimage semantically different (full per-operation entry
  instead of four op fields), so the document version is bumped.  A v1
  document is refused fail-closed with the named error
  region_schema_version_legacy (requested=1, available=2) instead of being
  reinterpreted under the v2 rules; any other version keeps
  region_schema_version_mismatch.
* validate_region_plan refuses a re-signed empty operations list with the
  named error region_operations_empty (previously the composition helper
  raised a bare ValueError); without a re-signed digest it is still caught as
  region_digest_mismatch.
* Tests: the round-1 fixture schema=1 / digest 626cc908... is rejected with
  and without replay; v2 documents are accepted; the empty-operations forgery
  yields region_operations_empty.  64 region tests, 307 with the existing
  execution suite.

The single-op path is untouched in this round; the 923a72e26 digest pins and
the CLI byte-comparison evidence stay valid (schema v2 only changes region
plan documents, which had no prior released artifact).

(cherry picked from commit 06910f99637c9f3143f433518be382a500a0f373)
